/* Clean (owner, 17 Nov): the third style, a layer over Soft. The chrome is black, white and one neutral grey ramp: surfaces,
   text, hairlines, the primary button in ink (black in light, white in dark, its own --dm-btn tokens), secondary buttons,
   switchers, knobs and toggles. Data and status keep Soft's colours: the blue accent for data, selection and links, the
   chart palette, agents' own colours and pastel avatars, and the vivid status colours (a green tick, never a black one;
   no red fill behind an error, only its red words and mark). Hairline outlines with a 1px contact shadow and one short soft shadow on cards; off-white
   head and foot strips; everything fully round: chips, tags, icon tiles, bars, tracks,
   rows and fields are pills or circles (the radii scale with --dm-rk-s, --dm-rk-m and --dm-r-tiny), and cards, panels and popovers
   take 22px round corners (--dm-rk-l), never squircles. Buttons have depth inside their fill: a blurred light along the top,
   a soft shade along the bottom and a near-solid edge; checkboxes and tracks have a soft inner shadow. In dark only, a faint
   neutral glow sits around the white primary button, never around cards (owner, 18 Nov; an approved exception to "no glows": white
   or neutral only, never a hue). Status colour only on small marks. Motion is calm: ease-out quint, hovers 150ms, presses
   at .97, menus scale and fade from their trigger, and a card rises 8px from .98 with its pieces 40ms apart (REVEAL.clean) */
:root[data-style="clean"],[data-style="clean"]{
